  <content>
  <section><div class="os-raise-extrasupport">
  <note>
    <para>The nth Term of Arithmetic Sequences<title>The nth Term of Arithmetic Sequences</title></para>
    <para><title/><!--Extra Support Name--> GENERAL TERM (NTH TERM) OF AN ARITHMETIC SEQUENCE</para>
  </note>
  <div class="os-raise-extrasupport-body"> 
    <!--Support Content-->
    <para>The general term of an arithmetic sequence with first term \(a_1\) and common difference \(d\) is: \(a_n=a_1+(n-1)d\).</para>
    <!-- Extra Support Content--> 
  </div>
</div>
<para class="os-raise-text-bold">Example 1</para>
<para>Write the explicit formula for the sequence given by the terms 18, 21, 24, 27, ...</para>
<para class="os-raise-text-bold">Solution: </para>
<para><emphasis>Step 1-</emphasis> Write the general formula.</para>
<para><emphasis>Step 2 -</emphasis> Substitute values for the first term, common difference/ratio, term number. </para>
<para>So, the explicit formula for the sequence 18, 21, 24, 27… is \(a_n = 18 + (n - 1)3\).</para>
<para>Now any term can more easily be determined - even the 1000th term!</para>
<para class="os-raise-text-bold">Example 2</para>
<para> Find the 15th term of a sequence where the first term is 3 and the common difference is 6. </para>
<para><emphasis>Step 1 - </emphasis>Write the general formula.</para>
<para><emphasis>Step 2 -</emphasis> Substitute values for the first term, common difference/ratio, term number. </para>
<para><emphasis>Step 3 -</emphasis> Simplify the expression. </para>
<para>If the explicit formula for this question was needed, we would not have substituted \(n = 15\) and the \(n\)th term formula would have been \(a_n = 3 + (n - 1)6\). This formula is also equivalent to </para>
<para>\(a_n = 3 + 6(n - 1)\). </para>
<title> Try It: The nth Term of Arithmetic Sequences</title>
<example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <para>Find the formula for the \(n\)th term of a sequence where the first term is 7 and the common difference is 9.</para>
  <para>Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.
    </para>
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
  <para>Here is how to find the 27th term of the sequence:</para>
  <para><emphasis>Step 1 -</emphasis> Write the general formula.</para>
<para><emphasis>Step 2 - </emphasis>Substitute values for the first term, common difference/ratio, term number. </para>

</solution></exercise>
</example></section>
